"0001856525-26-000054"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-1.5% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856525/000185652526000054/0001856525-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001856525-26-000054"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 0.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856525/000185652526000054/0001856525-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001856525-26-000054"},{"text":"Debt of $2.1bn against equity of $2.0bn. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856525/000185652526000054/0001856525-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001856525-26-000054"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.1% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856525/000185652526000085/0001856525-26-000085-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 19.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.19,"consecutive":2,"current":0.272,"current_display":"27.2%","threshold_display":"19.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -15.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","